###Setting up a proportion

Corresponding sides of similar triangles are proportional, so we can set up and solve a proportion:

$\dfrac{\blueE{HP}}{DP}=\dfrac{OP}{IP}$

We picked side $\blueE{\overline{HP}}$ because we need to find its length.

We picked side $\overline{DP}$ because it corresponds to side $\blueE{\overline{HP}}$.

Then we picked another pair of corresponding sides where we already knew the measurements.

$\begin{array}{rcl}
&\triangle HOP
\\
{\text{opposite to } \atop \angle I/\angle O}
&\overbrace{\underbrace{\!\!\!\!\!\left\{ 
\dfrac{\blueE{HP}}{DP}=\dfrac{OP}{IP}
\right\}\!\!\!\!\!}}
&{\text{opposite to } \atop \angle D/\angle H}
\\
&\triangle DIP
\end{array}$
